# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  PhonePe Android Forensics — .gitignore
#  NEVER commit acquisition data, generated reports, or the case registry.
#  These contain a real person's financial, social and identity PII.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Case registry — stores subject name, UPI id, investigator, and the local
# path to the acquisition. Created at runtime; must never be committed.
.pp_forensics/

# Raw Android acquisition / evidence (the subject's entire financial + social life)
com.phonepe.app/
data/data/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-journal
*-journal
*.7z

# Generated analysis output — every file here is full of the subject's PII
phonepe_evidence/
phonepe_analysis/
exports/
*_phonepe_evidence.html
*.export.csv

# Scratch / working files
scratchpad/
*.log

# Per-session run logs. These quote real values out of the acquisition under
# examination (transaction ids, amounts, counterparty counts) so they are working
# notes only — STATE.md and CONTINUE.md are the committable summaries.
# Session logs quote real subject values, so they stay out by default. Excluding
# the *files* rather than the directory matters: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a negation inside one can never re-include anything —
# and a cloned session is told to read the newest session log, which would then
# never be there.
notes/sessions/*
!notes/sessions/2026-08-09.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Editors / OS / tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
